							</p>
							<h3>Equalizer OEM Developer Kits</h3>
							  <p>Would your product or service benefit from equalizers befitting your brand? Would your customers enjoy better sounding personalization that allows them to control their own vibe?
							  </p>
							  <p>Our EQ portfolio ranges from low latency, low CPU utilization versions to no–compromise code that embodies the highest fidelity possible in the digital domain. Whether you’re looking for the best FIR or IIR EQs available, or simply a better version of the lightweight equalizer you have now, we have solutions that we know you’ll find to be exceptional.
							  </p>
							<h4>The Algorithmix Foundation</h4>
							  <p>Every equalizer in our portfolio descends from the research of Dr. Christoph Musialik, who spent years in deep analysis of the finest hardware equalizers. His research was not just theoretical, it was informed by real world implementations for Studer, Cadac, SSL, and other leading lights of our industry. The result is not modeling or simulation — no added noise, distortion, or inherited analog baggage — but true high resolution emulation: idealized digital implementations that outperform their analog antecedents in every measurable dimension, while preserving the musicality that made those originals legendary. All of our thEQ algorithms leverage 80 bit internal precision, delivering THD+N well below 24 bit quantization noise, and support sample rates from 44.1 kHz through 384 kHz for HRA and game audio workflows.
							  </p>
							<h4>Minimum Phase IIR</h4>
							  <p>Musical, versatile, CPU–efficient, our minimum phase IP encompasses the most complete collection of classic analog equalizer architectures ever assembled into a single codebase. Twelve distinct EQ personalities — ten serial and two parallel — span Classic Symmetrical, Proportional, Constant–Q, Parallel Feed–Forward/Feedback topologies, along with unique and proprietary topologies found nowhere else. This IP is available in three tiers:
							  </br>
							    <ul>
							      <li>A full–featured expression with twelve filter sections, per–section panorama control, live spectrogram, frequency snapping, and optional FiDef® psychoacoustic enhancement — suited to professional mixing and mastering applications.</li>
							      <li>A resource–efficient expression with a streamlined section count and reduced feature surface, optimized for products where CPU headroom, low latency, and ease of integration are priorities. This is the right choice for consumer personalization features, hardware DSP targets, and high channel count mixing environments.</li>
							      <li>A bespoke implementation unique to your application and needs, accommodating your hardware and memory requirements while exposing only the user controls you require.</li>
							    </ul>
							  </p>
							<h4>Linear phase FIR</h4>
							  <p>Transparency without compromise— For applications demanding absolute phase coherence and freedom from transient smear, our linear phase EQ IP sets the standard. The time–domain, two pass linear phase implementation is optimized for equalizing without leaving any sonic fingerprint. Processing artifacts fall well below –100dBFS. 
							  </p>
							  <p>Another linear phase implementation is tuned for aesthetic work, providing the artistic equalization that nudges material into sounding better without disturbing the time domain. Our frequency–domain LP codebase features VariSlope™, a proprietary filter technology enabling continuous shelf and cut slopes from near 0 to 24 dB per octave, including response shapes impossible to achieve with any classical filter design.
							  </p>
							  <p>Together, these two linear phase engines address every FIR use case. Combined with our minimum phase IIR offerings, MAAT’s EQ IP covers the full universe of professional equalizer requirements — from the lightest consumer touch to the most uncompromising mastering chain.
							  </p>
